  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale hotel**, owners and developers typically begin with the following global brand universe. Exact chain-scale classifications vary slightly by region and benchmarking firm, so this is best treated as a **commercial long list rather than a rigid ranking**. ([lodgingeconometrics.com](https://lodgingeconometrics.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Global-Brands-by-Chain-JUN2025.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Frequently shortlisted global brands\n\n| Hotel group | Core “hard brands” | Lifestyle, collection or conversion alternatives |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | Marriott Hotels, Sheraton, Westin, Renaissance, Le Méridien | Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio |\n| **Hilton** | Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Signia by Hilton | Curio Collection, Canopy by Hilton |\n| **Hyatt** | Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric | The Unbound Collection, JdV by Hyatt |\n| **IHG Hotels & Resorts** | Crowne Plaza, voco | Hotel Indigo, Vignette Collection |\n| **Accor** | Pullman, Swissôtel, Mövenpick, Grand Mercure | MGallery Collection |\n| **Radisson Hotel Group** | Radisson Blu | Radisson Individuals or Radisson Collection when a higher positioning is justified |\n\nHyatt, for example, explicitly identifies Hyatt Regency as upper-upscale and lists Marriott, Westin, Renaissance, Sheraton and Hilton as its principal competitors. Hyatt Centric and JdV are also positioned in upper-upscale, while Unbound spans upper-upscale through luxury. ([hyatt.com](https://www.hyatt.com/development/ourbrands/hyattregency?utm_source=openai))\n\nAccor’s principal premium brands are Pullman, Swissôtel, Mövenpick and Grand Mercure, while MGallery often enters the discussion for distinctive, design-led properties. ([assets.group.accor.com](https://assets.group.accor.com/yrj0orc8tx24/4bpCURWZXqOBx8dEYvSANx/1b76f77a967e522e3d496aff9d4e1f57/Why_Join_Accor_2026.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\nIHG places Crowne Plaza and voco in its premium portfolio, with Hotel Indigo and Vignette Collection positioned in luxury and lifestyle; in practice, all four can compete for upper-upscale projects depending on the asset and market. ([development.ihg.com](https://development.ihg.com/hotel-brands?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Brands often added regionally\n\nDepending on geography, the long list may also include:\n\n- **Europe:** NH Collection, Meliá Hotels & Resorts, INNSiDE by Meliá, Park Plaza  \n- **Middle East and Africa:** Rotana, Millennium, Dusit Thani, Avani, Minor Hotels brands  \n- **Asia-Pacific:** Pan Pacific, PARKROYAL Collection, New World Hotels & Resorts, Marco Polo, Nikko Hotels, Centara Grand  \n- **Greater China:** HUALUXE, Wanda Realm and selected domestic premium operators  \n- **Americas:** Delta Hotels, Wyndham Grand, Royal Sonesta and, for large convention assets, Gaylord Hotels  \n\n### Typical shortlist by project type\n\n**Conventional city or convention hotel**\n- Marriott Hotels\n- Hilton Hotels & Resorts\n- Hyatt Regency\n- Sheraton\n- Westin\n- Crowne Plaza\n- Pullman\n- Radisson Blu\n\n**Lifestyle-oriented new build**\n- Renaissance\n- Le Méridien\n- Canopy\n- Hyatt Centric\n- Hotel Indigo\n- MGallery\n\n**Conversion or distinctive independent hotel**\n- Autograph Collection\n- Tribute Portfolio\n- Curio Collection\n- The Unbound Collection\n- JdV by Hyatt\n- voco\n- Vignette Collection\n- MGallery\n\nCollection and conversion-oriented brands are particularly relevant when the owner wants to preserve the hotel’s identity or avoid the full physical standardization of a traditional hard brand. Hyatt describes Unbound as allowing properties to retain individuality, while IHG identifies voco and Vignette as conversion-friendly offerings. ([hyatt.com](https://www.hyatt.com/development/ourbrands/theunboundcollectionbyhyatt?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Practical “first-call” shortlist\n\nFor a typical internationally branded upper-upscale project, a balanced initial shortlist would normally be:\n\n1. **Marriott Hotels / Westin / Renaissance**\n2. **Hilton Hotels & Resorts / Curio Collection**\n3. **Hyatt Regency / Hyatt Centric**\n4. **Crowne Plaza / voco / Hotel Indigo**\n5. **Pullman / Swissôtel / Mövenpick**\n6. **Radisson Blu**\n7. One or two strong **regional operators**\n\nThe final shortlist is usually narrowed according to **territorial availability, management versus franchise structure, fees and key money, required development cost, room count, meeting-space intensity, loyalty-system contribution, conversion flexibility and the brand’s existing market representation**. A brand that is ideal conceptually may be unavailable because of an existing area of protection or pipeline commitment.",
